&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GraphQuon&lt;/strong&gt; is the annual Quebec–Ontario pre-SIGGRAPH workshop. The &lt;strong&gt;2025&lt;/strong&gt; edition ran &lt;strong&gt;15–16 November 2025&lt;/strong&gt; at the &lt;strong&gt;University of Toronto&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href="https://www.dgp.toronto.edu/graphquon/"&gt;series page&lt;/a&gt;). I &lt;strong&gt;presented&lt;/strong&gt; there with &lt;strong&gt;Sheldon Andrews&lt;/strong&gt; (ÉTS): &lt;strong&gt;Where to Wear?&lt;/strong&gt; — how frictional contact leaves a readable history on surfaces, and how we can turn that into graphics and engineering feedback. &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://antoineboucher.info/CV/blog/posts/graphquon-2025-university-of-toronto/"&gt;Version française&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>